Subject: [PATCH] wireless/bcmf: log bounded raw association event state

When the existing opt-in Broadcom frame trace is enabled, record numeric
authentication event fields and the local association/carrier state before
the interface-up early return. It decodes the 16-bit event flags through the
existing bcmf_getle16 accessor, matching the driver's event-field decoding.
This captures events that arrive before MAC counters or socket setup begin.

This is diagnostic instrumentation only. It does not establish a performance
baseline or change authentication completion, carrier decisions, retries,
timeouts, or other policy. The line contains no interface name, address,
SSID, key, payload, or pointer. The existing verbose wireless logs remain
unchanged and must not be enabled merely to collect this record.

diff --git a/drivers/wireless/ieee80211/bcm43xxx/bcmf_driver.c b/drivers/wireless/ieee80211/bcm43xxx/bcmf_driver.c
--- a/drivers/wireless/ieee80211/bcm43xxx/bcmf_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/wireless/ieee80211/bcm43xxx/bcmf_driver.c
@@ -622,6 +622,18 @@ void bcmf_wl_auth_event_handler(FAR struct bcmf_dev_s *priv,
   status = bcmf_getle32(&event->status);
   reason = bcmf_getle32(&event->reason);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211_BROADCOM_FRAME_TRACE
+  wlwarn("BCMF_AUTH_EVENT type=%" PRIu32 " status=%" PRIu32
+         " reason=%" PRIu32 " flags=%u pending=%u waiter=%u up=%u"
+         " running=%u\n",
+         type, status, reason,
+         (unsigned int)bcmf_getle16(&event->flags),
+         (unsigned int)priv->auth_pending,
+         (unsigned int)(priv->auth_signal != NULL),
+         (unsigned int)priv->bc_bifup,
+         (unsigned int)IFF_IS_RUNNING(priv->bc_dev.d_flags));
+#endif
+
   wlinfo("Got auth event %" PRId32 " "
          "status %" PRId32 " reason %" PRId32 " from <%s>\n",
          type, status, reason, event->src_name);
